Again I disagree here. Getting protection later is much more costly in
time and effort. Also you have to carry the extra weight in armor around
fighting tougher monsters because of XL while you do it. Doing the MPR at
low XLs unbalances the game in the players favor:

1) Low XLs make it cheaper to get the protection. So you get it faster.

2) Low XLs keeps the level of monsters generated low. In addition there
is a total mismatch between low level monsters and a completely buff XL9
pet.

3) Getting protection earlier means that you can ditch the heavy armor
required to keep up with the dungeon earlier.

Leveling up generally only gives one benefit for a character that's not
trying to kill monsters, and that's extra PPs. I've outlined how to gain
HPs without leveling up, and weapons slots are not so critical that you
cannot do it later in mid game. As I've said on numerous occasions it's
tough to stay XL2 or XL3 with the geometric progression on XPs. One floating
eye or one small mimic will take you from XL2 to XL5 in a couple of hits.

