So you believe that the extra HP acts as a buffer against that first surprise
attack. I agree with you to a point. But I find that it comes at the cost of
having a lot stronger normal attacks against that buffer. And until you finish
building your protection, it's at a high AC.  I simply don't see
rothes, and killer bees, and soldier ants in the MPR. Once I get the extra
AC, each of these are a lot less dangerous than before.

>Eliminate instadeaths ruthlessly.  In the early game, every /fire,
>/lightning, rolling boulder, etc is a potential instadeath.

But they are relatively low risk events in the early game. And for each of
these, that buffer only saves you from the first hit. Any monster with with
what I call a $175 AGO (a good one) wand is likely to get two or three
cracks at you. Even a wand of striking can be devistating.

